  "narrative": "The newly delivered discovery wave is largely null after considering direction, uncertainty, clinical magnitude, and multiplicity. Because all estimates are already signed to each claim direction, I treat positive signed values as supporting the registered negative-direction hypothesis (raw exposed-minus-comparator more negative/stronger dependency) and negative signed values as opposing it. Most point estimates are far below the approximate 10%-of-outcome-magnitude screen, intervals cross zero, and many upper signed bounds remain below the relevant threshold; those are rejected or deferred rather than accepted. H31 is the notable exception: R27 gives a signed estimate of about -0.028 for feature_047 absence vs presence on outcome_008, with a 95% interval excluding zero on the negative signed side. That means the raw effect is positive, i.e. feature_047=0 has less negative dependency than feature_047=1, opposite the registered direction -1 claim. The raw magnitude is very near, not clearly above, the 10% screen, and this is one nominal interval among many unadjusted comparisons, so I reject H31 in its registered direction rather than accept it. Because H31 is the only non-null signal in this wave and could represent a reproducible opposite association, I request validation on H31 and register a reversed proposal for the same comparison with direction +1. H32, H37, H38, and H43 are rejected for their original directions because either the point estimates are small/opposite or the signed intervals provide no plausible support above the clinical threshold in the hypothesized direction. H33, H39, H40, H41, H42, H27, and H28 remain unresolved because their intervals include zero and/or allow effects above threshold, but the evidence is too weak for acceptance. H28 remains active as a borderline positive candidate if the H31 validation does not establish a meaningful reversed effect. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "State after iteration 3 appraise: no accepted claims. The latest feature_047/feature_008/feature_060/feature_034 wave adds many null or borderline results. H31 is the only discovery interval excluding zero, but it supports the opposite of the registered negative claim and is only at/marginally below the 10% magnitude screen. Original H31 is rejected; a reversed proposal is registered and H31 is sent for validation. H28 is retained as an active borderline positive candidate. Most other candidates are deferred because intervals include zero and point estimates are below clinically meaningful magnitudes. Continue interpreting all results as dataset-specific associations; avoid causal or generalizable language.",
